---
description: Governs the Vue 3 + TypeScript + Vite project configuration, defining the technology stack and build setup.
globs: "{vite.config.*,tsconfig.*,package.json,env.*,.env*}"
---
- Framework: Vue 3 with Composition API (script setup).
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode enabled).
- Build Tool: Vite.
- State Management: Pinia (when global state is needed).
- Router: Vue Router 4.
- HTTP Client: Axios.
- Testing: Vitest + @vue/test-utils.
- Architecture: Front-end and back-end separation (API-only consumer, no SSR).
- The backend API base URL must be configured via Vite environment variables (VITE_API_BASE_URL in .env files), never hardcoded.
- TypeScript strict mode must be enabled in tsconfig.json.
- Path aliases (e.g., @ -> src/) should be configured in both vite.config.ts and tsconfig.json.
